# Build context hygiene. The image needs the code, the brief and the crate
# registry; it must never carry a run's leftovers, a fleet's home, or a
# database of anything.
volumes/
# The volume images live beside volumes/, preallocated and large: never source, never context.
volume-images/
endurance/runs/
tests/
docs/
site/

# **Except the vehicle.** `docs/deep_research/vehicle/` is the configuration the reference console
# serves, and the `vehicle` compose service bakes it into the image at `/opt/vehicle`. The rest of
# `docs/` stays out on purpose: it is the corpus and the design record -- sixteen thousand lines of
# prose that no container needs, and the one folder in this repository that is *evidence* rather than
# runtime. An `!` line has to follow the pattern it un-ignores, and re-including a subdirectory of an
# ignored one is the only way to say "this part of `docs/` is program".
!docs/deep_research/vehicle/

.git/
.github/
# The two lines' governance: design reasoning and the vehicle's records, never the fleet's to read.
governance/
.scratch/
# The smoke stack builds after it prepares, so its scratch root is beside the context.
.smoke-*/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# The registry itself is mounted at run time, not baked: it is large, it is
# versioned on the host, and an image that carried it would need rebuilding
# every time a crate is added.
vendor/.cargo-home/
vendor/kitchen/target/

.env
*.log

# Patterns are anchored at the context root, so `tests/` above leaves these in. The harness's,
# recorder's and pump's tests never reach an image, nor what the harness tests leave behind.
harness/tests/
harness/session_context.json
harness/tombstones/
recorder/tests/
pump/tests/
